    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **James Wood** leading the charge. Occupying the leadoff spot against Alcantara, his 70.34 efficiency score is buoyed by a significant +10% order bonus and a favorable matchup against a 4.45 xERA arm; his 85% stolen base probability against a slow-delivering pitcher makes him our priority engine for the scarcest category. **Trevor Story** (71.87) and **Corbin Carroll** (69.70) represent our most balanced elite plays. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a high-level catcher and a pitcher who holds runners well, his dynamic platoon edge and order placement keep him in \"Strong\" territory. Meanwhile, **Trevor Story** benefits immensely from wind-aided conditions and a generous 4.56 xERA matchup, making him a prime candidate to anchor our power production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Cole Young** (42.70) on the bench. He sits just shy of our rotation threshold, narrowly eclipsed by **Alex Freeland**, whose switch-hitting utility and recent form provided a slightly higher floor against Elder. We are also monitoring **Seiya Suzuki** (44.29) closely; while he is currently active, his score is severely depressed by a daunting matchup against deGrom. Should the wind patterns shift or the matchup outlook worsen, he is the most likely candidate to be swapped for a bench asset. Finally, note that while **Vinnie Pasquantino** is a strong start at 64.21, his +14% platoon edge is the primary driver keeping him relevant today; we are betting heavily on his ability to capitalize on a favorable look at Hanifee to offset the risks posed by other lower-ceiling options like **Dalton Rushing** or **Alex Freeland**.",
